# NestJS Backend Guidelines

Use NestJS with Prisma and PostgreSQL.

Prefer:
- one module per feature
- DTOs with class-validator
- explicit controllers and services
- database constraints in Prisma schema
- OpenAPI decorators on endpoints and DTOs

Avoid:
- repositories over Prisma without need
- CQRS / event sourcing
- microservices patterns
- unnecessary shared "core" layers

Auth in v1 is single-user JWT (see docs/decisions/001-single-user-auth.md).

Protect domain endpoints with JwtAuthGuard.
Keep /health and /auth/login public.
